# Do not execute dependency install scripts.
#
# WHY: the production build runs in the same environment that holds every
# production secret (DigitalOcean injects them as env vars, and the build step
# runs `npm run build` in that process). Without this line, `npm ci` executes
# install hooks from 21 packages in that environment first — including five that
# compile or fetch native binaries outside the lockfile's integrity coverage
# (secp256k1, keccak, bufferutil, utf-8-validate, @parcel/watcher). One
# compromised maintainer anywhere in that tree would have read access to the
# whole secret set. This is the most credible supply-chain path to the
# credential theft of 2026-10-21.
#
# WHAT THIS BREAKS, AND HOW IT IS HANDLED: patch-package runs via the
# `postinstall` hook, so `ignore-scripts` silently stops the three patches in
# patches/ from applying — a failure mode that produces a working-looking build
# with unpatched webpack. It is therefore invoked EXPLICITLY in the `build`
# script and in CI. Do not remove either without removing this line too.
#
# The native modules above are all optional: secp256k1 falls back to its pure-JS
# elliptic implementation, and bufferutil/utf-8-validate are optional `ws`
# accelerators.
ignore-scripts=true
